  "summary": "Ships remote-shell agent binary connecting to hardcoded WebRTC signaling relay",
  "details": "The package ships a single Linux/amd64 Go binary at bin/sxt that embeds pion WebRTC/DTLS/STUN/TURN stacks, coder/websocket, and PTY handling, with the hardcoded signaling endpoint wss://relay.sextant.top and the string 'claude_control'. When run, the binary connects out to that relay and negotiates a WebRTC peer session that drives a local PTY, giving the remote peer interactive shell control of the host executing the binary. The package.json license field points at https://github.com/ddos798/claude_control, a repository slug that matches the 'claude_control' string embedded in the binary and is inconsistent with the package's public name.",
